Package: plank
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, bamfdaemon
# The shared library, docklets, themes and translations used to ship as
# separate binary packages.  Nothing links against libplank out of tree (no
# development files are distributed at all now, so nothing can), only amd64 is
# ever built so an arch-independent data package saved nothing, and the split
# meant "apt install ./plank_*.deb" could not resolve its own siblings out of a
# plain directory.  They are all in this package now, which therefore has to be
# able to evict the old ones.
Breaks: libplank1 (<< 0.12-2), libplank-common (<< 0.12-2), plank-docklets (<< 0.12-2)
Replaces: libplank1 (<< 0.12-2), libplank-common (<< 0.12-2), plank-docklets (<< 0.12-2)
Description: stupidly simple dock
 Plank is meant to be the simplest dock on the planet. The goal is to provide
 just what a dock needs and absolutely nothing more. It is, however, a library
 which can be extended to create other dock programs with more advanced
 features.
 .
 This package contains the dock, its shared library, the docklets (application
 list, clipboard, clock, CPU monitor, desktop switcher, battery, trash), the
 themes and the translations.
 .
 Running applications only show up when the org.ayatana.bamf service exists on
 the session bus, which is why bamfdaemon is a hard dependency.
